ingredients:
  - "1 1/2 cup rice flakes"
  - "1 medium tomato (chopped)"
  - "2 tsp oil"
  - "1 small capsicum (chopped)"
  - "1 small carrot (chopped)"
  - "1 small onion (chopped)"
  - "1/2 small cabbage (chopped)"
  - "6 French beans (chopped)"
  - "2 dsp groundnuts"
  - "2 green chilies (chopped)"
  - "1/2 tsp mustard seeds"
  - "Few curry leaves"
  - "Salt to taste"
instructions:
  - "Chop all vegetables."
  - "Soak flaked rice in water for 1 minute, then strain and set aside."
  - "Heat 1 tsp oil in a pan, roast groundnuts, and keep aside."
  - "Heat remaining oil, add mustard seeds, curry leaves, and chilies, then sauté onions until golden brown."
  - "Add chopped vegetables and fry until they soften."
  - "Mix in soaked flaked rice, salt, and stir-fry for 1-2 minutes."
  - "Add roasted groundnuts and mix well."
  - "Serve hot."
